  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts are most commonly known by a few specific names:\n\n1. **Terminal Tackle** \u2013 The Columbia PFG Terminal Tackle T-Shirt is made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. It features Omni-Wick\u2122 advanced evaporation and Omni-Shade\u2122 UPF 50 sun protection, drying quickly and managing moisture to keep you cool and dry.\n\n2. **Tidal Tee** \u2013 The Tidal Tee is the women's version of the Terminal Tackle PFG shirts. It features lightweight moisture-wicking fabric.\n\n3. **Bahama** \u2013 Featuring angler-friendly details and lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun so you can stay out there longer.\n\n4. **Tamiami** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric.\n\n5. **Tidal Deflector / Terminal Deflector** \u2013 The Tidal Deflector (women's) and Terminal Deflector (men's) are designed for cooling, made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology using touch-activated cooling fabric to prevent overheating.\n\nThe most popular of these for being ultra-thin and breathable are typically the **Terminal Tackle** and **Bahama** styles. The PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style.",
